"""Register the StackRouter power.status live read (N2181).

The StackRouter's live read, following the N2145/N2146/N2147/
N2148/N2149/N2150/N2151/N2152/N2153/N2154/N2155/N2156/N2157/N2158/
N2159/N2160/N2161/N2162/N2163/N2164/N2165/N2166/N2167/N2168/N2169/
N2170/N2171/N2172/N2173/N2174/N2175/N2176/N2177/N2178/N2179/N2181 pure-row
pattern. N2142's live loop stamps frame["power_status"] each tick --
but the StackRouter (surge-router) has NO driver at all: it
extends DuctRouter (StackRouter.java:11), not a factory or crafter or
bridge or conveyor, so no existing driver matches it -- the
N2178/N2179/N2181 drivers' implementation lists hold "ItemBridge" /
"LiquidBridge" / "StackRouter" only, exact-string matches, so
"StackRouter" never matches them. Its StackRouterBuild.updateTile
unloads items at a rate that follows the folded efficiency
(StackRouter.java:29, `float eff = enabled ? (efficiency +
baseEfficiency) : 0f;`, with StackRouter.java:35, `progress +=
eff;`) -- so a surge-router with no power would unload slower and
draw no glow, as if power.status were 1.0. N2181 adds the pure
power row (source_stack_router_power_status_row_state) on a new
family state file, its own driver
(source_stack_router_tick_buildings_state, the item-bridge /
liquid-bridge / stack-conveyor N2178/N2179/N2181 precedent), its
own frame key ("source_stack_router_building", added to N2142's
SOURCE_CONSUMER_FRAME_META_KEYS), and the simulate_factory wiring,
folded by the shared machinery into the min efficiency
(BuildingComp.java:1969-1976, ConsumePower.efficiency is
build.power.status) so the unload rate (StackRouter.java:29-35)
and the glow (StackRouter.java:79-81) follow it.

Composition, not re-implementation: the shared efficiency
machinery (SourceBuildingEfficiencyState.update_consumption_state,
via update_consumption_non_optional_pass_state) already folds
{"result": ..., "is_power": true} rows into the min efficiency.
N2181 does not touch it. N2181 supplies the missing pure power
row + the driver fold + the frame key + the simulate_factory
wiring; no new consumer rows. No has_consumers fix is needed: the
machinery runs only when the block has a power consumer, and the
power consumer counts toward hasConsumers (Block.java:1449).
The stack router's power draw is STATIC, not conditional:
`consumePower(3f / 60f);` (Blocks.java:2266) registers a plain
ConsumePower -- the catalog consumePower 0.05 is present and the
plain radar gate (block.properties.has("consumePower")) works.
The pure row is the same ConsumePower read
(`return build.power.status;`, ConsumePower.java:39).
StackRouterBuild has NO shouldConsume override, so the
BuildingComp default applies (BuildingComp.java:755-756, `return
enabled;`), and updateConsumption forces efficiency to zero when
the gate is false (BuildingComp.java:1960 + 1992-1994). There is NO
gate to defer here (unlike the ItemBridge / LiquidBridge link
gates in N2178/N2179): the power-only fold is EXACT for this
family, because the only gate is `enabled`, which the driver
already checks. The surge def carries `baseEfficiency = 1f;`
(Blocks.java:2265) -- so the coupling is NOT a hard gate:
updateTile computes `eff = efficiency + baseEfficiency` when
enabled, so at efficiency 0 (no power) the router still unloads
at eff 1f, and power raises eff toward 2f and lights the glow
(StackRouter.java:79-81, `if(glowRegion.found() && power !=
null && power.status > 0){` with `Draw.color(glowColor,
glowAlpha * power.status);`). The proof's
efficiency_zero_at_no_power key proves the folded efficiency is
0 -- it must NOT claim the router stops; the glow is the only
hard power gate on this family. Note the disabled branch differs
from the conveyor: StackRouter computes `... : 0f;`
(StackRouter.java:29) where StackRouter computes `... : 1f;`
(StackRouter.java:270) -- a disabled surge-router unloads
nothing, while a disabled surge-conveyor still reels at eff 1f.
No updateTile advance: the eff fold / progress advance / unload
branch / target handoff / current-pick branch (StackRouter.java:
28-70) waits for its own slice; the proof carries no progress /
unloading / target / acceptItem keys. The stack router's static
power consumer is the only modeled consumer, so the folded
efficiency is the min over the modeled consumers (power only).
Single def (surge-router, consumePower 3f/60f, Blocks.java:2266);
size 1, speed 6f, itemCapacity 10, health 130, surge-alloy 5 /
tungsten 1. No family split: surge-router is the ONLY StackRouter
def (Blocks.java:2255). duct-router is a DuctRouter
(Blocks.java:2193) and router / distributor are Routers
(Blocks.java:2139/2144), all with NO consumePower def and NO
hasPower line, so their transport does NOT depend on
power.status -- they are explicitly OUT of scope; the driver's
implementation list holds "StackRouter" only, and the plain radar
gate enforces the same split on the def side. Catalog quirk:
duct-router and router list consumesPower true and hasPower true
in the catalog despite NO consumePower def and NO hasPower line
in Blocks.java, the same pattern as plastanium-conveyor in N2181
-- the plain radar gate is what matters.
"""
